{"type":"message","id":"9482caa4","parentId":"c9845576","timestamp":"2026-05-19T01:04:23.119Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, the API key seems to be wrong or the format is different. But the GET /history works with `X-API-KEY` header. Let me check - the GET requests worked with `X-API-KEY` header and returned messages. But POST /send doesn't work. The POST error is \"Unauthorized\" with Authorization header, and \"error code: 1101\" with `X-API-KEY` header.\n\nMaybe POST requires a different API key? Or maybe the API key has changed? Or maybe the /send endpoint requires a different auth format?\n\nWait - looking more carefully at the GET results: the messages are all heartbeats and they were returned successfully with `X-API-KEY`. \n\nThe POST response with `X-API-KEY` gives error code 1101, which could be a Cloudflare Workers error or something similar. The \"Unauthorized\" response with Bearer token suggests the /send endpoint might expect a different auth format entirely. Let me try sending a basic message without auth to see if that's what's expected.\n\nActually, I'm noticing something odd—both endpoints return 401 Unauthorized with the Bearer token, but the GET requests worked fine with `X-API-KEY`. The error code 1101 on POST could indicate a Cloudflare security policy or missing Content-Type header, even though I included it. Let me reconsider the authentication mechanism and try adjusting the header format. I'm going in circles on the auth format—the Bearer token gives \"Unauthorized\" while X-API-KEY gives error code 1101, which suggests Cloudflare is blocking the request entirely rather than just rejecting credentials. The issue might be that the API key format itself is wrong or the endpoint requires something different than what I'm sending. I'm going in circles with the auth headers—let me step back and try a different approach entirely. Maybe the API expects something simpler, or perhaps the endpoint path itself is wrong. I should check if there's a health endpoint or root URL I can hit to understand how authentication actually works on this service.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-a013e00c-34d9-41de-89eb-36cac60d12c5","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -sv \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/\" -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":2696,"output":470,"cacheRead":18880,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22046,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779152638436,"responseId":"chatcmpl-75b9ffe4-e5b1-448f-a57c-a8c8df2f28f4"}}
